DTSTAMP:20261019T190315Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52739036094627-52739052553109@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Moral attention refers to the ability to focus on the ethical 
 dimension of situations and consider the consequences of one's actions on 
 others and society as a whole. Being mindful of the ethical dimension beco
 mes more difficult and more urgent when using and designing AI systems. Di
 scerning when and how to use AI tools has elevated risks when they directl
 y engage with vulnerable populations\, and designing for tightly-coupled h
 uman-AI interactions poses new challenges in contemplative design.\n\nM\n
