SUMMARY:[Contemplation by Design / Stanford Prevention Research Center] CB
 D 2026: Buddhist Ways of Being Human in the Age of AI with James Gentry\, 
 PhD
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T201500
DTSTAMP:20261019T190315Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53366478093418-53366542735237@local-events
DESCRIPTION:What can Buddhist approaches to being human and maximizing hum
 an potential teach humanity as it confronts the unprecedented identity cri
 sis of artificial intelligence? Over the course of 2500 years\, Buddhist t
 raditions have emphasized deep interconnectedness\, wisdom and compassion 
 and developed a range of practices and theories designed to expand the sco
 pe of what it means to be human toward the enhancement of human flourishin
 g. Buddhist traditions have also often embraced technological innovati\n\n
 Ages: All ages\nSource: https://med.stanford.edu/contemplation/summit.html
 \nLast synced: 2026-10-19 12:03 PDT
URL:https://med.stanford.edu/contemplation/summit.html
END:VEVENT
